# Prompts

Every prompt sent to a paid API (Gemini) lives in `PROMPTS.md`, keyed by a `## section_id` heading. Python loads it with `load_prompt("section_id")`. Do not embed long system prompts in `.py` files.

When adding a new paid call: add a `##` section in `PROMPTS.md`, then reference that id from code. Placeholders like `{seed}` stay in the markdown file.

Do not log prompts together with secrets. API keys come from env (`GEMINI_API_KEY`), never from source.
